<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Brazilian</p>
<p>soccer matches played at the weekend:</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> Aracatuba		  1    Botafogo-Ribeirao Preto  0</p>
<p> Corinthians		3    Santos			 1</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira  1    Portuguesa		   2</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		 1    Juventus		     0</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista    3    Guarani			2</p>
<p> Rio Branco		 2    America-S.J.Rio Preto    0</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		  0    Sao Jose		     0</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	   0    Palmeiras		    0</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 13  8  5  0 35 12 29</p>
<p> Portuguesa		13  6  5  2 32 22 23</p>
<p> Santos		    13  6  4  3 22 17 22</p>
<p> Guarani		   13  4  5  4 25 30 17</p>
<p> Juventus		  13  3  4  6 23 27 13</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  13  2  6  5 18 28 12</p>
<p> Botafogo		  13  0  8  5  8 15  8</p>
<p> America		   13  1  3  9  9 30  6</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     13  8  3  2 32 16 27</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 13  5  7  1 20 11 22</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		13  5  5  3 18 17 20</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  13  4  5  4 17 15 17</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira 13  4  4  5 20 23 16</p>
<p> Rio Branco		13  3  6  4 17 20 15</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 13  3  4  6 12 18 13</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   13  3  4  6 16 23 13</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for</p>
<p>the final play-off stage. If teams are level on points,</p>
<p>positions are decided by the number of games won.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, second stage</p>
<p> Botafogo		   2    Flamengo		     2</p>
<p> Bangu			0    Vasco da Gama		0</p>
<p> Fluminense		 2    Volta Redonda		1</p>
<p> Madureira		  3    Americano		    5</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Botafogo		   2  1  1  0  3  2  4</p>
<p> Fluminense		 2  1  1  0  3  2  4</p>
<p> Americano		  2  1  0  1  5  4  3</p>
<p> Flamengo		   1  0  1  0  2  2  1</p>
<p> Bangu			1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    1  0  1  0  0  0  1</p>
<p> Madureira		  2  0  1  1  4  6  1</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    1  0  0  0  1  2  0</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>Botafogo won the first stage.</p>
